    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0419" n="331" xml:id="pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/3587: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-07-27T19:00:00-05:00">July 27, 1933—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>120. The first meeting of the Mixed Commission composed of delegates of the
                    opposition and delegates of the three political parties took place this
                    afternoon. I commenced the proceedings with a brief address emphasizing again
                    the salient features of President Roosevelt’s message to the Cuban people<anchor
                        n="29" xml:id="d287-f1"/> as made public on July 1st. The meeting was
                    significant in that for the first time in 3 years constructive discussion
                    between members of the opposition and of the Government’s adherents took place.
                    A distinctly patriotic and satisfactory spirit was shown by both sides and
                    agreement was reached on several important features of the constitutional reform
                    as proposed. The next meeting of this Commission will be held tomorrow and every
                    day subsequently under my chairmanship until a final agreement is reached.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
